<onlyinclude>'''Distributed artificial intelligence''' (DAI) studies how multiple computational entities coordinate intelligent activity, including reasoning, planning, learning and distributed problem solving.

== Explanation ==
Several autonomous robots may share observations and divide a mapping task rather than send all decisions to a single computer. Distribution creates opportunities for parallelism and local knowledge but adds communication, synchronization and conflict-resolution problems.

